(Problem & goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Breast cancer risk calculators return a percentage that many users find either meaningless) Tj
T*
(or frightening—neither reaction reliably drives appropriate follow-up. This app adds a 2–3) Tj
T*
(minute conversational layer: explain the number in plain language, branch on elevated vs) Tj
T*
(average risk, and motivate concrete next steps without diagnosing or impersonating a) Tj
T*
(clinician.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Theories chosen & operationalization) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Health Belief Model \(HBM\) — Rosenstock, 1974; updated in breast screening literature) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why: HBM predicts preventive action when people perceive susceptibility and severity) Tj
T*
(*accurately*, believe benefits outweigh barriers, and feel capable of acting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In the dialogue \(shared/dialogue.ts\):) Tj
T*
(- Elevated branch: Calibrate severity \(“most women with this estimate do *not* get) Tj
T*
(cancer”\); cue to action \(clinician visit in 2–4 weeks\); surface barriers \(cost, false) Tj
T*
(alarms\); build self-efficacy \(“you’re already taking a helpful step”\).) Tj
T*
(- Average branch: Reassure without false certainty; cue routine mammography; affirm) Tj
T*
(existing healthy behaviors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Fagerlin et al. risk-communication principles — *Med Decis Making* 2007) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why: Absolute risks with denominators \(e.g., “2 in 100”\) outperform relative-only framing) Tj
T*
(for comprehension and appropriate worry.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In the dialogue: Opening script and system prompt require absolute risk + age-matched) Tj
T*
(comparator; forbid “double your risk” without absolute numbers. In the implemented) Tj
T*
(prototype, the nci-natural-frequency-001 evidence chunk \(National Cancer Institute — see) Tj
T*
(EVIDENCE_REGISTER.md\) grounds this natural-frequency framing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Motivational Interviewing \(OARS\) — Rollnick, Miller & Butler, 2008) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why: Direct persuasion increases resistance in health contexts; MI elicits change talk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In the dialogue: Elevated branch ends with open questions \(“What would help you take the) Tj
T*
(next step?”\); chat suggestions are user-paced; assistant reflects rather than commands.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Avatar choice: “Maya” — warm female health educator) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Selection criteria \(research-informed\):) Tj
T*
(- Trust & warmth: Health messages from perceived-credible, empathetic presenters increase) Tj
T*
(recall and reduce defensive processing \(source: health communication meta-literature;) Tj
T*
(ACS/NCI patient-education tone\).) Tj
T*
(- Role clarity: Introduces self as AI health educator, not a clinician—reduces authority) Tj
